S += [P('0. What we are building, in one paragraph', H1),
      P('The verified core stays untouched: one lock as the source of truth, the stint fixed-effects estimator, exact one- and two-stop enumeration, compound offsets, pit-loss handling, the post-race replay, and the 11-weekend, 29-case evidence base (0.023 against 0.137 s/lap, 28 of 29). On top of it we build the <b>Race Twin</b>: pick a race, a driver, an intervention lap, a compound and a continuation; the engine replays the driver\'s own race with only the tyre plan replaced, shows the lap-by-lap source of the difference, the cumulative elapsed-time delta with uncertainty, and two moving blips on the circuit. Three fidelity modes behind one interface: <b>tyre-only</b> (swap the curve, reset the age), <b>fixed-context</b> (add in-lap, pit loss, stationary time, out-lap, warm-up, safety-car rules, the rest of the plan; the scientifically strongest mode and the default), and <b>frozen-field</b> (rivals follow their observed race; the ghost catches traffic, takes dirty air, gets DRS, attempts passes sampled probabilistically; rival strategic responses are not simulated). The claim scope is written into every output: single-car, iso-context, virtual race-time position on the driver\'s own trajectory; never a predicted finishing position except in frozen-field mode, and there with a distribution.'),
      P('Wording that goes on the screen, verbatim: <i>Ghost Strategy Replay. A lap-by-lap estimate of how the same driver\'s race-time trajectory changes when only the tyre plan is replaced. Under fixed weather, flags and driver-and-car baseline, Orb v1 estimates the alternative plan would have completed the race N seconds sooner. Single-car pace counterfactual; rival reactions, overtakes and resulting traffic are not simulated in this mode. Generated from a pre-race model trained without this weekend; evaluated against a leave-one-driver-out Sunday reference.</i>', SM)]
md('## 0. Programme\nVerified core untouched. Race Twin on top: three fidelity modes (tyre-only, fixed-context default, frozen-field), claim scope written into every output.\n')
