# ---------- 12 questions ----------
QA = [('How do you validate something that never happened?', 'We validate the parts that did happen: for every real tyre change in sealed weekends we hide the laps after the stop, predict the response, and score it. Unchosen strategies are reported as model-implied counterfactuals under a held-out post-race reference, with regret against the hindsight oracle, never as observed outcomes.'),
      ('Is it not circular to pick the plan and score it with the same model?', 'The pre-race policy and the post-race scorer are separated. The target weekend is excluded from training, the target driver is excluded from the Sunday reference where data allows, and the holdout was sealed by a metadata rule before this layer was tuned.'),
      ('Why does a different stop not change traffic?', 'In fixed-context mode it does not, by construction, and the screen says so. Frozen-field mode adds traffic, dirty air, DRS and passing against rivals on their observed trajectories; what it still does not simulate is rivals changing strategy in response.'),
      ('Is the second dot physically simulated?', 'Its timing is modelled; its geometry is the driver\'s own recorded trajectory projected onto track distance and time-warped. It is a pace twin, not a vehicle-dynamics simulation, and the pit lane uses the recorded pit path.'),
      ('Do you use race data in the pre-race recommendation?', 'No. Every pre-race scenario carries a forecast cutoff and a hash; race data enters only afterwards, for scoring and audit.'),
      ('Why can the ghost be ahead on the map but not "in P6"?', 'Because in fixed-context mode the map shows virtual race-time position on the driver\'s own trajectory. Position claims are made only in frozen-field mode, and there as a distribution with its range.'),
      ('What is the uncertainty on the ghost?', 'Whole curves and parameters are sampled, not per-lap noise, so adjacent laps stay correlated: degradation curve, transfer, pit loss, out-lap, warm-up, offsets, and in frozen-field mode passing outcomes. The halo is the 10th to 90th percentile of the ghost\'s position; the readout gives the probability of gain.'),
      ('How large is the untouched sample, really?', 'It is counted in races and driver-race cases, not telemetry rows. The sealed holdout is at least six whole weekends from 2023 to 2025, chosen by rule; the prospective case is Madrid. The 29 existing cases are cross-validated, and we call them that.'),
      ('What happens under a safety car?', 'The observed schedule is fixed in both worlds. Normal pace gains are frozen during controlled laps, thermal state keeps updating, pit loss switches to the SC value, and a restart warm-up applies. An SC-aware mode that recomputes the stop decision carries a warning because restart traffic would differ.'),
      ('If the frozen-field simulator is not calibrated by Sunday, what do we show?', 'Fixed-context mode, which is the scientifically strongest one anyway, with the elapsed-time delta, its band and the probability of gain. The fidelity switch shows frozen-field as unavailable rather than pretending.')]
S += [P('12. Ten questions this feature must survive', H1)]
for i, (q, a) in enumerate(QA, 1): S += [KeepTogether([P(f'<b>{i}. {q}</b>', B), P(a)])]
md('## 12. Ten questions\n' + '\n'.join(f'**{i}. {q}**\n\n{a}\n' for i, (q, a) in enumerate(QA, 1)))
doc = SimpleDocTemplate('out/Orb_v1_Roadmap_v3.pdf', pagesize=A4, leftMargin=1.8 * cm, rightMargin=1.8 * cm, topMargin=1.6 * cm, bottomMargin=1.6 * cm, title='Orb v1 Race Twin roadmap v3', author='Team Orb v1')
def footer(c, d): c.saveState(); c.setFont('Helvetica', 7.5); c.setFillColor(colors.HexColor('#6B7280')); c.drawString(1.8 * cm, 1 * cm, 'Orb v1 Race Twin · roadmap v3 · draft for critique'); c.drawRightString(A4[0] - 1.8 * cm, 1 * cm, str(d.page)); c.restoreState()
doc.build(S, onFirstPage=footer, onLaterPages=footer); open('out/ROADMAP_v3.md', 'w').write('\n'.join(MD)); print('built')
